T15:59:29Z","closed_at":"2026-06-29T15:58:40Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in v4.7.rc.custom_build [71011704c]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.rc (71011704c) - macOS Tahoe (26.5.1) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Apple M4 Pro - Apple M4 Pro (14 threads) - 24.00 GiB memory - CoreAudio (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWith the following GDScript file:\n```gdscript\n@static_unload\n\nfunc test() -> void:\n    print(\"Hello\")\n```\nthe entire file (including the `test()` function) is highlighted via the LSP as having the `REDUNDANT_STATIC_UNLOAD` warning:\n\n<img width=\"269\" height=\"102\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f7417224-bb8c-4875-9bad-e3ddef73f979\" />\n\nIt makes sense that instead only the `@static_unload` annotation should be highlighted/underlined as code causing the warning.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAdd the following GDScript file to a project:\n```gdscript\n@static_unload\n\nfunc test() -> void:\n    print(\"Hello\")\n```\nNote how the entire file is highlighted as having a warning, instead of just the first line causing the warning.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/